Development 2.4.0 / native ABI epoch 5 (validation in progress)
====================================================================

- Start a deliberate rebuilt native cohort: libXm, libMrm and libUil use
  libtool 5:0:0. Header/runtime epoch checks accompany changed widget/source
  records. No compatibility alias to the preceding SONAME is provided.
- Validate XIM preedit spans, resulting lengths, conversion and caret bounds
  before replacing composition buffers.
- Add ICU scalar/grapheme coordinate maps without changing source-scan scalar
  counting. Share ICU paragraph bidi and HarfBuzz line captures across text
  drawing, metrics, carets, hits, selections and wrapped composition.
- Add native semantic providers and optional AT-SPI D-Bus transport with
  explicit ownership, bounded text ranges and multiple-shell support.
- Add focused fork documentation and source-pinned strict documentation CI.
  Source availability, focused fixtures and installed-cohort acceptance remain
  separate; see docs/status.md for the current validation boundaries.


Development 2.4.0 / native ABI epoch 6 (validation in progress)
====================================================================

- Advance Xm/Mrm/Uil together to libtool 6:0:0 for changed native text context
  records and public accessibility value/provider records. Rebuild every native
  consumer; no alias for an older SONAME is supplied.
- Bound per-widget grapheme resolver and font/shaping leases with retained
  capture ownership and explicit configuration invalidation.
- Follow documented Xft column metrics in Text, TextField and DataField.
- Expose ScrollBar numeric values/actions/events and custom value providers.
- Repair input-method transport lifetime and committed/preedit ordering; add
  isolated real IBus/m17n composition and service-reconnection fixtures.

Development 2.4.0 / numeric action parameter parsing
======================================================

- Parse numeric representation action parameters with range-checked `strtol`,
  rejecting overflow before narrowing to `int` while preserving legacy prefix
  syntax.
- Add a regression and maintenance documentation for the conversion boundary.

Development 2.4.0 / ClipWindow translation storage
====================================================

- Grow generated ClipWindow translation tables on demand with checked size
  arithmetic instead of concatenating into a fixed 1000-byte buffer.
- Add an installed-library ScrolledWindow regression and maintenance notes.

Development 2.4.0 / picture repeat-count parsing
=================================================

- Check picture repeat counts before narrowing them to `int`, treating
  negative and overflowing values as ordinary input instead of using invalid
  counts in graph-copy operations.
- Extend the picture regression and document the parser boundary.

Development 2.4.0 / PrintShell resolution parsing
==================================================

- Parse the printer server resolution with a bounded conversion, preserving
  screen-resolution fallback for missing, malformed, non-positive, or
  overflowing values.
- Add an installed-library parser regression and documentation.

Development 2.4.0 / FontSelector font-string bounds
====================================================

- Honor the destination size while building FontSelector XLFD strings and
  guarantee termination for short buffers.
- Add a public-widget regression and maintenance documentation.

Development 2.4.0 / XmString multibyte conversion bounds
=========================================================

- Use checked `size_t` lengths and bounded copies when converting compound
  strings to multibyte text, rejecting component-size overflow before
  allocation.
- Add a conversion regression and maintenance documentation.

Development 2.4.0 / RowColumn accelerator storage
==================================================

- Grow generated RowColumn accelerator strings on demand with checked size
  arithmetic instead of writing into a fixed stack buffer.
- Add a public MenuBar regression and maintenance documentation.

Development 2.4.0 / constructor argument-count guards
======================================================

- Reject Scrolled Text and List argument counts that would overflow internal
  `Cardinal` additions before merging or allocating argument arrays.
- Add direct maximal-count regressions and documentation.

Development 2.4.0 / dialog constructor count guard
===================================================

- Reject the maximum `Cardinal` argument count in `XmeCreateClassDialog`
  before adding the shell argument and allocating the merged list.
- Add a direct maximal-count regression and documentation.

Development 2.4.0 / dialog argument-count guards
=================================================

- Reject maximum `Cardinal` counts in Command and MessageBox constructors
  before adding their internal dialog-type argument.
- Add direct maximal-count regressions and documentation.

Development 2.4.0 / compound-text length checks
