DataField selection conversion bounds (2026-10-24)
===================================================

- Accumulate multi-fragment selection text lengths with checked `size_t` arithmetic and reject values that cannot fit the existing DataField `int` length contract before allocation or replacement. Protect wide-character buffer sizing and report failed conversions cleanly.
- Represent empty or unconvertible text-property lists with an allocated empty buffer, preserving selection ownership, locale conversion behavior, public interfaces and native ABI. Extend the DataField selection regression and document the bounds contract in `docs/datafield-selection-bounds.md`.
- Native AArch64 validation passes the rebuilt `check-selection-timestamp` regression, including DataField `XA_STRING` conversion.

JPEG and PNG image allocation bounds (2026-10-24)
=================================================

- Validate decoded dimensions, pixel counts and row sizes before allocating JPEG and PNG image buffers, preventing integer wraparound from creating undersized storage. Treat JPEG allocation failure as a normal image-load error instead of entering the scanline loop with a null buffer.
- Preserve valid image formats, public image-loading APIs, display-depth handling and native ABI. Document the allocation contract in `docs/image-loader-bounds.md`.
- Native AArch64 validation passes the image-scaling and malformed-image regression suite.

TextField preedit recovery ownership (2026-10-24)
==================================================

- Keep the base address of the multibyte recovery buffer while scanning past completed characters, avoiding an invalid interior-pointer free during overstrike inline preedit updates. Stop safely when locale conversion or a multibyte boundary is invalid.
- Preserve composition behavior, preedit callbacks, widget resources, public interfaces and native ABI. Document the ownership rule in `docs/textfield-preedit-recovery.md`.
- Native AArch64 validation passes the TextField source build and XIM preedit-range regression; the optional font-backed preedit-state fixture was unavailable on the minimal rpi4 image.

TextField clear-selection bounds (2026-10-24)
==============================================

- Validate the selected span before converting it to the existing `int` insertion-length contract, preventing `span + 1` wraparound in `clear-selection`. Protect the wide-character replacement allocation before multiplying by `sizeof(wchar_t)`.
- Preserve normal selection replacement, callbacks, cursor behavior, public interfaces and native ABI. Document the bounds contract in `docs/textfield-clear-selection-bounds.md`.
- Native AArch64 validation passes the warning-enabled TextField source build; the former `ClearSelection` out-of-bounds warning is absent.

Text selection-array allocation bounds (2026-10-24)
===================================================

- Check the configurable Text selection-array element count before multiplying by `sizeof(XmTextScanType)`. Invalid counts now fall back to Motif's built-in scan table instead of wrapping the allocation size.
- Preserve scan-type traversal, resource/API contracts, widget ownership and native ABI. Document the fallback in `docs/text-selection-array-bounds.md`.
- Native AArch64 validation passes the warning-enabled TextIn source build.

Text key-selection parameter initialization (2026-10-24)
==========================================================

- Initialize `key-select` cursor and range values before action-parameter conversion, so unknown direction names become a harmless no-op instead of reaching selection scanning with uninitialized state.
- Preserve valid horizontal/vertical action behavior, selection resources, callbacks, public interfaces and native ABI. Add `tests/automated/check-text-key-selection.c` and document the behavior in `docs/text-key-selection-parameters.md`.
- Native AArch64 validation passes the invalid-parameter regression under Xvfb.

DataField insert-string action bounds (2026-10-24)
